1
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:11,167
Under four occupied homes in Building B,
the cast-iron waste line is being
replaced.

2
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:18,028
Three hundred twelve feet of new pipe,
routed under kitchens and baths.

3
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:25,423
This work happens inside people's homes,
so it is planned around the people who
live there.

4
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:33,931
Lines are located, floors protected, and
dust walls go up. Then, a narrow saw-cut
trench, two feet wide.

5
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:40,900
New Schedule 40 ABS goes in, sloped a
quarter inch per foot.

6
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:46,633
Every line is filled and held for a water
test before anything is covered.

7
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:55,097
Then backfill, new concrete, and finishes
patched to match.

8
00:00:55,350 --> 00:01:00,528
And at the end of every working day, each
home has a working toilet and sink.

9
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:06,448
Phased unit by unit, so residents stay
home throughout.
